; examples/quoted-list.nx — quoted compound collections, step #8c.1.
;
; The quoted list is constructed at runtime via the internal
; `#%list` primitive (emitted by `lowerQuotePayload` for any
; compound list payload). Elements are recursively
; quote-lowered: symbols intern via the VM Interner, keywords
; same, fixnums use the literal Tiny variant.
;
; Syntax-quote `\`(a ~b)` and splicing `~@xs` sit on top of this
; same runtime substrate (see syntax-quote.nx).

(defn point [x y] (quote (point x y)))

; Result: the data list (point x y) — NOT a call. quote
; preserves the structural form as a runtime list value.
(point 3 4)
